"subs": [
{
"t": 0.15,
"dur": 5.682,
"text": "The boss wrote three words on the report: “like family.” The most expensive words of his life."
},
{
"t": 6.132,
"dur": 8.681,
"text": "Die at work, on the clock, and it's a workplace accident. They have to pay. Inspectors would ask why the time clock has no clock-out button."
},
{
"t": 15.064,
"dur": 8.057,
"text": "So that night, the boss filled out the report himself. Changed two ten to five a.m. Changed “at the factory” to “at home.”"
},
{
"t": 23.37,
"dur": 7.168,
"text": "Loc's wife hadn't made it up from the countryside. The boss signed as the reporter, too. Relationship: “like family.”"
},
{
"t": 30.789,
"dur": 3.071,
"text": "Team lead Hong stood behind the door. Saw everything."
},
{
"t": 34.11,
"dur": 1.833,
"text": "Whatever the paper says, that's the truth."
},
{
"t": 36.543,
"dur": 2.249,
"text": "Five a.m.… that's a cursed hour."
},
{
"t": 39.192,
"dur": 3.066,
"text": "What's a cursed hour? I'll tell you next time. Follow along."
}
],
